{"name":"Pick of the Litter","hex":"#b8a49b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pick of the litter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The best person or item in a group; the best that one has to offer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pick_of_the_litter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pick of the Litter (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Pick of the Litter  is a 2018 American documentary film by Dana Nachman and Don Hardy about a two-year odyssey following puppies training to be guide dogs for the blind. It had its world premiere at the Slamdance Film Festival in January. A web television series of the same name inspired by the film and following a new group of dogs was released on Disney+ on December 20, 2019."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2f/Pick_of_the_Litter_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pick_of_the_Litter_(film)","wikidata":"Q56551002"},{"title":"Pick of the Litter (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Pick of the Litter  is a Japanese shōjo manga series written by Yuriko Suda that was serialized in Monthly Asuka from 2004 through 2007. The individual chapters were published in six tankōbon volumes by Kadokawa Shoten."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ef/Potl_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pick_of_the_Litter_(manga)","wikidata":"Q3544363"},{"title":"Pick of the Litter (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Pick of the Litter  is an American documentary television series by Dana Nachman and Don Hardy for Disney+ based on the 2018 film of the same name, also written and directed by the duo, that began streaming on December 20, 2019."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Pick_of_the_Litter_Title.png/330px-Pick_of_the_Litter_Title.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pick_of_the_Litter_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q79298461"},{"title":"Litter","blocks":[{"text":"Litter consists of waste products that have been discarded incorrectly, without consent, at an unsuitable location. The waste are objects, often man-made, such as aluminum cans, paper cups, food wrappers, cardboard boxes or plastic bottles, but also large and hazardous items of rubbish such as tires, electrical appliances, electronics, batteries and large industrial containers are sometimes dumped in isolated locations, such as national forests and other public lands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Littering_in_Stockholm.jpg/330px-Littering_in_Stockholm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Litter","wikidata":"Q1780867"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/New_Orleans_Litter.jpg/500px-New_Orleans_Litter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/New_Orleans_Litter.jpg/1280px-New_Orleans_Litter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/New_Orleans_Litter.jpg/500px-New_Orleans_Litter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Litter in New Orleans, Louisiana.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_Orleans_Litter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/1280px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/